From 6c2dbcd278ac9cf932aa9129e826cb431f61cf17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban show: an expired quota wall reads '(reset
 passed)', not 'starts on its own when that wall resets'

PR #1865 review nit 2 (t_01a1d31b227be614, review 5885960246): once a pinned_quota_wall skip's `until` has passed
and no later tick has replaced it, pool_replace_helps offers the pool re-place, but the same `kanban show` text still
read "quota-walled until HH:MMZ ... It starts on its own when that wall resets". The two halves contradicted.

- kanban_dispatch_skip: new _wall_passed(skip, now), the exact complement of the pool_replace_helps suppression.
  words(skip, now=) appends " (reset passed)" after the until stamp; advice(skip, now=) / sentence_advice drop
  "starts on its own when that wall resets" for it ("that wall's reset has passed; the next dispatcher tick
  re-checks the pin ..."). A future, missing or unparseable until keeps today's wording.
- kanban_queue_position.local_words(place, now=): one `now` (default time.time()) feeds pool_replace_helps, words
  and the skip advice, so both halves agree at the boundary (until == now counts as passed on both).
- kanban_parent_unclaimed: ready_hint threads its `now`; post_notice uses the payload's observed_at for the queue
  words and pool hint, and notice_advice defaults to that observed_at when the notice is rendered later.

Proof: 8 new cases RED on the #1865 head (expired wall: no marker, reset clause present; signature for now=), GREEN
after; 27 importer/notice test files: 661 passed; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
